{"name":"Strawberry Wine","hex":"#cb6a6b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strawberry wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting strawberries instead of grapes, resulting in a light or medium-bodied wine with a sweet and tart flavor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strawberry_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit wine","blocks":[{"text":"Fruit wines are fermented alcoholic beverages made from a variety of base ingredients ; they may also have additional flavors taken from fruits, flowers, and herbs. This definition is sometimes broadened to include any alcoholic fermented beverage except beer. For historical reasons, cider and perry are also excluded from the definition of fruit wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg/330px-%D5%86%D5%BC%D5%A1%D5%B6_%D5%A3%D5%AB%D5%B6%D5%AB.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_wine"},{"title":"Strawberry Wine (Deana Carter song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Strawberry Wine\" is a song written by Matraca Berg and Gary Harrison, and recorded by American country music artist Deana Carter. It was released on July 26, 1996 as Carter's debut single and the first from her debut album, Did I Shave My Legs for This? The song became a number 1 hit on both the US Billboard Hot Country Singles & Tracks chart and the Canadian RPM Country Tracks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/StrawberryWineDeanaCarter.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_Wine_(Deana_Carter_song)"},{"title":"Strawberry","blocks":[{"text":"The garden strawberry is a widely grown hybrid plant cultivated worldwide for its fruit. The genus Fragaria, the strawberries, is in the rose family, Rosaceae. The fruit is appreciated for its aroma, bright red colour, juicy texture, and sweetness. It is eaten either fresh or in prepared foods such as jam, ice cream, and chocolates. Artificial strawberry flavourings and aromas are widely used in commercial products. Botanically, the strawberry is not a berry, but an aggregate accessory fruit. Each apparent 'seed' on the outside of the strawberry is actually an achene, a botanical fruit with a seed inside it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg/330px-Garden_strawberry_%28Fragaria_%C3%97_ananassa%29_single2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG/250px-Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Elderberryfruit5081.JPG/250px-Elderberryfruit5081.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elderberries, a common fruit wine ingredient.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElderberryfruit5081.JPG"},{"srcse